cuems-engine (0.1.0rc4-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Merge rc_1 into debian/bookworm (source moved 52 files since 0.1.0rc3-1);
    bump upstream version 0.1.0rc1 -> 0.1.0rc4 to match.
  * PORT_HANDLER: make the port-exclusion list actually exclude (869ed9wf7).
    add_config_ports() passed set_ports() the same dict object it already
    held, so the `previous_ports == ports` guard was an identity check that
    always returned early and _all_used_ports stayed permanently empty — the
    engine could draw its own oscquery_ws_port (9190). Ports are now split
    into reservations (validated), config declarations (cannot raise) and
    system observations (cannot raise); the system scan is port-based via
    `ss -tuln` so it sees other users' sockets; draws reserve atomically and
    are bind-probed before being handed out. add_system_ports()/
    add_config_ports() moved to BaseEngine so the controller gets them too.
  * cuems-engine-mock: carry forward the no-op rsync shim and cuems-node-engine
    PATH drop-in introduced on rc_1 as 0.1.0rc2-3 (that entry is not in this
    changelog — it was added on the rc_1 line after 0.1.0rc3-1 forked).
    Retains the cuems-<component> wrapper names from 0.1.0rc3-2; the stale
    audioplayer-cuems/dmxplayer-cuems mock scripts are removed.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 21:00:00 +0200

cuems-engine (0.1.0rc3-2) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * cuems-engine-mock: rename drop-in wrapper binaries to match the new
    cuems-<component> convention (audioplayer-cuems -> cuems-audioplayer,
    dmxplayer-cuems -> cuems-dmxplayer); the mock package now ships
    /usr/bin/cuems-audioplayer and /usr/bin/cuems-dmxplayer
  * cuems-engine-mock: Conflicts: now covers cuems-dmxplayer as well
    (previously only cuems-audioplayer, so dmxplayer conflict was missing)
  * cuems-engine-mock.postinst: correct install-path message (/usr/bin/ not
    /usr/local/bin/) and use the new binary names

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Thu, 16 Apr 2026 20:55:00 +0200

cuems-engine (0.1.0rc3-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * merge rc_1 into debian/bookworm (47 commits):
    - rename player binary references: audioplayer-cuems -> cuems-audioplayer
      and dmxplayer-cuems -> cuems-dmxplayer (kill scripts, PlayerHandler
      pgrep filter, mock wrappers, docstrings, dev test settings.xml)
    - remove stale dev/cuems-node-engine.service (production unit in
      cuems-common is the single source of truth)
    - cue enable/disable toggle via WebSocket OSC; skip disabled cues in
      nextcue/GO/arming/auto-chains
    - arm: wait for in-progress arm instead of failing on concurrent access
    - plus additional bug fixes and test coverage improvements from rc_1

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Thu, 16 Apr 2026 20:35:00 +0200

cuems-engine (0.1.0rc2-2) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * cuems-engine-mock: fix wrapper install path from /usr/local/bin to /usr/bin
    - /etc/cuems/settings.xml configures player paths under /usr/bin/
    - wrappers at /usr/local/bin/ were never found by the node engine

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Wed, 11 Mar 2026 13:00:00 +0100

cuems-engine (0.1.0rc2-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Fixed EngineStatus initialization order bug
    - Initialize _recieved before test property to prevent AttributeError
  * Fixed OSCQuery GIL crashes
    - Disabled ALL OSCQuery callbacks to prevent GIL crashes from C++ threads
    - Implemented polling loop for safe command value change detection (100ms)
    - Python thread safely checks for command value changes
    - Commands auto-reset after execution for next trigger
  * Added comprehensive OSCQuery debugging
    - Enhanced logging for endpoint creation and node management
    - Debug output for status endpoint building process
  * JACK/PipeWire compatibility
    - Maintains no_start_server=True for proper systemd/PipeWire integration
    - Requires PipeWire JACK libraries via LD_LIBRARY_PATH

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Thu, 22 Jan 2026 17:50:00 +0100

cuems-engine (0.1.0rc1-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian package release
  * Engine infrastructure for CUEMS system
  * Controller and node engines for media playback
  * MIDI and OSC communication support
  * Integration with cuems-utils virtual environment
  * Systemd service support
  * Console scripts: node-engine, controller-engine, system-ports

